+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Voyage 1 Intent
+
+Build a TodoMVC app per `assets/app-spec.md` using the base markup at `assets/app-template.index.html`. Vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors, persists to localStorage.
+
+## Specs Written
+
+- `features/todo-crud.feature` - 12 scenarios: create, edit, delete, toggle, focus
+- `features/toggle-all.feature` - 3 scenarios: mark all complete/active, checkbox sync
+- `features/counter.feature` - 4 scenarios: active count with pluralization
+- `features/clear-completed.feature` - 4 scenarios: remove completed, visibility
+- `features/visibility.feature` - 2 scenarios: main/footer hide/show
+- `features/routing.feature` - 5 scenarios: #/, #/active, #/completed filters
+- `features/persistence.feature` - 4 scenarios: localStorage round-trip
+
+Total: 35 scenarios, 168 steps.
+
+## Watchbill
+
+Six watches in order: visibility-and-creation, item-interactions, toggle-all, counter-and-clear, routing, persistence.
+
+## Next Step
+
+Dispatch QM. QM writes step definitions and verification support, then dispatches Crew for production code.
diff --git a/features/clear-completed.feature b/features/clear-completed.feature
