--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/clear-completed.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+Feature: Clear completed todos
+  As a user
+  I want to remove all completed todos at once
+  So that I can clean up my list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes completed todos
+    Given the user has a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks "Clear completed"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no completed todos
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when completed todos exist
+    Given the user has a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is visible
+
+  Scenario: After clearing, toggle all checkbox resets
+    Given the user has a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks "Clear completed"
+    Then the "Mark all as complete" checkbox is not checked
diff --git a/features/counter.feature b/features/counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..713125a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+Feature: Active todo counter
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many todos are left
+  So that I know my remaining workload
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows zero items when no active todos
+    Then the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows singular for one active todo
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows plural for multiple active todos
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter excludes completed todos
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2412b10
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+Feature: localStorage persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my data
+
+  Scenario: Todos survive page reload
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user reloads the page
+    Then a todo "Buy groceries" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Completed state persists across reload
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user toggles the checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    And the user reloads the page
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is marked as completed
+
+  Scenario: Multiple todos persist across reload
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Buy milk" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user reloads the page
+    Then a todo "Buy groceries" appears in the list
+    And a todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Deletion persists across reload
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Buy milk" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user clicks the destroy button for "Buy groceries"
+    And the user reloads the page
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not in the list
+    And a todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..799ad80
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Route-based filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todos by status using URL routes
+  So that I can focus on relevant items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+    And the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has a completed todo "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: All route shows all todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is visible in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is visible in the list
+    And the "All" filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is visible in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is not visible in the list
+    And the "Active" filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not visible in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is visible in the list
+    And the "Completed" filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo hides it in Active filter
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the user toggles the checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not visible in the list
+
+  Scenario: Reopening a todo hides it in Completed filter
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    And the user toggles the checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not visible in the list
diff --git a/features/todo-crud.feature b/features/todo-crud.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cb328b7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-crud.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+Feature: Todo creation and editing
+  As a user
+  I want to create, edit, and remove todos
+  So that I can track my tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+
+  Scenario: New todo is created on Enter
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then a todo "Buy groceries" appears in the list
+    And the new todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: New todo trims whitespace
+    When the user types "  Buy groceries  " in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then a todo "Buy groceries" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Empty todo is not created
+    When the user presses Enter with an empty new todo input
+    Then no todo is added to the list
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only todo is not created
+    When the user types "   " in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then no todo is added to the list
+
+  Scenario: New todo input is focused on page load
+    Then the new todo input has focus
+
+  Scenario: Double-click activates editing mode
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    And the edit input contains "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves on Enter
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user changes the edit input to "Buy milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is not in the list
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves on blur
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user changes the edit input to "Buy milk" and blurs
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Editing discards on Escape
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user changes the edit input to "Buy milk" and presses Escape
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" appears in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+
+  Scenario: Editing trims whitespace
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user changes the edit input to "  Buy milk  " and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Editing with empty text destroys the todo
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not in the list
+
+  Scenario: Clicking checkbox toggles completion
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user toggles the checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is marked as completed
+    When the user toggles the checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not marked as completed
+
+  Scenario: Clicking destroy removes the todo
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user clicks the destroy button for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not in the list
diff --git a/features/toggle-all.feature b/features/toggle-all.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b8cccb6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle-all.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+Feature: Toggle all todos
+  As a user
+  I want to mark all todos as complete or active at once
+  So that I can manage my list efficiently
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all marks all todos as completed
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user toggles the "Mark all as complete" checkbox on
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is marked as completed
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is marked as completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all marks all todos as active
+    Given the user has a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user toggles the "Mark all as complete" checkbox off
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not marked as completed
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is not marked as completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all checkbox reflects individual states
+    Given the user has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user toggles the checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the "Mark all as complete" checkbox is not checked
+    When the user toggles the checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the "Mark all as complete" checkbox is checked
